# API

Skill: `data-layer`. Stack: axios `apiClient`, central `ENDPOINTS`, RTK thunks/slices.

## Do

- Declare paths in `endpoints.ts` (`ENDPOINTS`), not as string literals in components or slices.
- Call HTTP through `apiClient` from `axios.ts` (shared interceptors and auth).
- Reuse the existing `apiClient` instance instead of creating another axios client.
- Group domain methods next to neighbors (`tasksApi`, `userApi`):

```ts
export const tasksApi = {
  getList: () => apiClient.get<TasksListResponse>(ENDPOINTS.tasks.list),
  claim: (id: string) =>
    apiClient.patch<TaskClaimResult>(ENDPOINTS.tasks.claim(id)),
};
```

- Keep response/body types under `types/` and import them with `import type`.
- Re-export from `index.ts` when neighboring domains do.
- Invoke API from store thunks, loaders, or Feature orchestration instead of UI primitives.
- Add a new endpoint in this order: `ENDPOINTS` -> api method -> thunk/loader.

## Checklist

- [ ] Path lives in `ENDPOINTS`
- [ ] Method uses `apiClient` in `<domain>.ts`
- [ ] Types live in `types/`
- [ ] Errors follow `errors.mdc`
- [ ] Feature/store/loader owns the call; UI primitives only render
